     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Deploying mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together blocks exfiltration, and no single control does. Phishing is always available and gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user, so mfa:user never blocks anything. Stopping pivot_internal needs segmented plus patched:workstation plus patched:laptop, which is 3 controls. Without that, the attacker reaches the internal network, authenticates to ciserver, kerberoasts to get stolen_admin, and escalates ciserver using stolen_admin regardless of patches. Leaking ciserver secrets then gives stolen_dbadmin, which cannot be prevented. The only remaining barrier is the db, fileserver and backup auth step. It is blocked only when mfa:dbadmin is deployed and the attacker cannot get admin_dc or admin_adfs. Getting admin_dc or admin_adfs requires auth_dc or auth_adfs, which mfa:admin blocks. So mfa:admin plus mfa:dbadmin is sufficient.\"}"
    }
   ],
